# CODEOWNERS for the product repository.
#
# The repository owner fills this in from the control repository's docs/workstreams.yaml: one line
# per workstream path with the prefix product: removed, owned by the GitHub username of the
# developer who holds that workstream (workstreams.yaml records the developer's handle; map each
# handle to a GitHub username). Then rename this file to .github/CODEOWNERS.
#
# The product rulesets require 0 approvals (the gating review is the approval), so CODEOWNERS
# requests reviews and shows ownership; it does not block a merge. Later lines take precedence.

# Default owner of everything not listed below.
*               @REPLACE-WITH-OWNER-GITHUB-USERNAME

# One line per workstream, for example:
# /web/         @REPLACE-WITH-UI-DEVELOPER
# /api/         @REPLACE-WITH-BACKEND-DEVELOPER
# /infra/       @REPLACE-WITH-INFRA-DEVELOPER

# CI and repository settings stay with the repository owner.
/.github/       @REPLACE-WITH-OWNER-GITHUB-USERNAME
/tools/         @REPLACE-WITH-OWNER-GITHUB-USERNAME
